  "notes": [
    "autodesign-start is the only public skill at install time.",
    "Stage 09 keeps canonical and visual reference repair available, then implements Pencil, DS, prototype, QA, handoff documentation, and reconcile report workflows after selected visual references are approved.",
    "Pencil-derived records require a completed active Pencil MCP handoff: get_editor_state, batch_design, export_nodes, an Autodesign-owned virtual .pen filePath, created/exported node bindings, and real canvas export paths.",
    "Externally supplied JSON is never the sole trust source; evidence must cross-check the virtual Pencil filePath plus actual export file bytes.",
    "Primitive inventory, DS tokens/contracts, prototype metadata, semantic QA, and max-two-refinement records are deterministic metadata artifacts.",
    "Stage 09 handoff writes JSON and Markdown documentation only under autodesign/outputs/handoff and does not generate frontend source files or executable prototype code.",
    "Stage 09 hooks are observational/advisory only and do not generate artifacts, call image generation, call Pencil MCP, mutate design files, or produce frontend code.",
    "Eval report and skill optimization remain later-stage outputs."
  ]
}
